      "content": "That sounds promising. So, instead of saying \"the sample size was limited due to X,\" we could say something like, \"We purposefully utilized a highly controlled, intensive cohort of 12 participants to maximize data granularity and ensure high-fidelity neuro-imaging captures\"? Do you think that kind of wording would be enough to pivot the conversation away from the statistical power issue entirely?",
